pragma solidity 0.8.28;

/**
 * @title MorphoVaultV2Bytecode
 * @notice Verbatim creation bytecode of Morpho's Vault V2 contracts, so tests can run the REAL vault
 *         implementation inside the local EVM instead of an ERC4626 mock.
 * @dev Robinhood Chain's Morpho deployment is Vaults V2 (not MetaMorpho V1/V1.1). Vault V2 has
 *      behaviours no generic ERC4626 mock reproduces - `max*` views hardcoded to 0, a decimal offset
 *      derived from the asset, interest that is rate-limited by `maxRate` rather than tracking raw
 *      balances, and share/asset gates. Testing `MorphoVaultsStrategy` against a mock therefore proves
 *      very little; testing it against this bytecode proves the strategy works against what is
 *      actually deployed.
 *
 *      PROVENANCE
 *      - Source:    https://github.com/morpho-org/vault-v2
 *      - Commit:    b1e9005c5d7a1c99eaa909dde02a365886faac07 (2026-07-31)
 *      - Contracts: src/VaultV2.sol:VaultV2
 *                   src/periphery/gates/WhitelistReceiveSharesGate.sol:WhitelistReceiveSharesGate
 *      - Compiler:  solc 0.8.28, via_ir = true, optimizer = true, optimizer_runs = 100000,
 *                   evm_version = "cancun", bytecode_hash = "none"
 *                   (i.e. the repository's own `[profile.default]`, so this is the artifact their
 *                    release build produces)
 *
 *      TO REGENERATE
 *      1. git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/morpho-org/vault-v2
 *      2. Copy `src/VaultV2.sol`, `src/interfaces`, `src/libraries` and `src/periphery/gates` into a
 *         bare foundry project carrying the compiler settings listed above (the rest of `src`
 *         - adapters and imports - needs the morpho-blue/metamorpho submodules and is not used here).
 *      3. `forge build`, then take `.bytecode.object` from `out/VaultV2.sol/VaultV2.json` and
 *         `out/WhitelistReceiveSharesGate.sol/WhitelistReceiveSharesGate.json`.
 *
 *      The bytecode is held by small deployer contracts rather than the test contract itself so each
 *      blob is deployed exactly once and stays clear of the EIP-170 runtime size limit.
 *      NOTE: `MorphoVaultV2Deployer` lands at ~23.3KB of the 24.576KB limit. If a future Vault V2
 *      release grows past that, `forge build --sizes` will flag it and the constant has to be split
 *      across two deployer contracts and concatenated before `create`.
 */

